---
import Page from "../../layouts/Page.astro";
---
<Page
  title="Charts"
  dek="A chart shows you how to do one specific thing: set something up, measure it, or fix it."
>
  <div class="prose">
    <p class="empty">There are no charts yet.</p>
    <p>
      Each chart will be written alongside the tool or fix it describes, so it only ever describes something that
      exists and has been tried. Until then there's nothing honest to write a guide about.
    </p>
    <h2>What a chart will look like</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>One task per chart, named for the job: what you'll have when you're done.</li>
      <li>What you need before you start: hardware, operating system, engine version.</li>
      <li>Every command you need to run, in order, and what you should see after each one.</li>
      <li>How to undo it.</li>
      <li>Why it works, briefly, so you can adapt it when your setup differs.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      If you'd like to write one when the time comes, start with the <a href="/contributing/">contributing guide</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</Page>
<style>
  .empty {
    font-size: var(--step-2);
    font-stretch: var(--stretch-sign);
    font-weight: 750;
    line-height: 1.25;
  }
</style>
